WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:04.260
Effektive makes effectful code easier to
write and read.

00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:08.320
This workflow activates a user without
Effect wrappers or generators.

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:10.920
Find a user.

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.470
If already active, return it.

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:17.065
Otherwise, create the active record, save
it, and return the result.

00:00:17.905 --> 00:00:21.495
The compiler infers the failures and
service operations.

00:00:21.495 --> 00:00:24.585
A missing user ends the workflow before
any write.

00:00:25.703 --> 00:00:29.263
The code on the right is actual compiler
output.

00:00:29.263 --> 00:00:34.425
It preserves evaluation order, typed
failures, and the required Users service.

00:00:35.415 --> 00:00:38.825
Independent validation and strict
TypeScript checking pass.

00:00:39.785 --> 00:00:43.525
Four runtime paths match a handwritten
Effect reference:

00:00:43.525 --> 00:00:48.185
activation, unchanged active user, missing
user, and storage failure.

00:00:49.465 --> 00:00:51.665
You write the workflow.

00:00:51.665 --> 00:00:54.576
The compiler produces checked Effect code.
